{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1537848-w20-berserker-frenzy-ending","id":1537848,"title":"[W20] Berserker Frenzy ending","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-28T20:58:48-07:00","id":1537848,"title":"[W20] Berserker Frenzy ending","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> How does the Berserker merit work when the werewolf needs to leave the frenzy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berserker W20 Core p. 476</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have uncanny control over your inner anger, and<br /> can use your Rage as most Garou cannot. <b>You can enter<br /> a berserk frenzy at will, ignoring your wound penalties.</b><br /> You still suffer the consequences of any actions commit-<br /> ted in the throes of frenzy. When circumstances might<br /> cause you to frenzy, you must make a standard roll to see<br /> if you do so or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frenzy W20 Core p. 261</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves frenzy in two ways:<br /> <b>\u2022 Berserk Frenzy: The werewolf can only see<br /> moving targets \u2014 targets she wants to reduce to bloody<br /> lumps of mangled meat. A berserk Garou shifts im-<br /> mediately to either Crinos or Hispo form (the player<br /> decides which), and attacks something.</b><br /> Whom she attacks depends on the circumstances.<br /> If the Garou\u2019s permanent Rage does not exceed her<br /> permanent Gnosis, she will not tear into her packmates<br /> \u2014 unless she\u2019s in the Thrall of the Wyrm. Anything else<br /> is fair game, including other were-creatures who are not<br /> members of her pack.<br /> A Garou whose permanent Rage exceeds his per-<br /> manent Gnosis attacks anything that moves. He can\u2019t<br /> distinguish between targets unless his player spends a<br /> Willpower point, in which case he can select his victim.<br /> If he doesn\u2019t have the Willpower to spare, the Storyteller<br /> chooses who he attacks. <b>Werewolves in this state don\u2019t<br /> remember what happens to them during frenzy. Many<br /> collapse once the frenzy is over.</b><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <b>A werewolf can only come out of frenzy once the trig-<br /> gering situation is over. Once he\u2019s escaped, the player rolls<br /> Willpower (difficulty equaling the Garou\u2019s own Rage) to<br /> escape the frenzy. If the roll fails, the player can try again<br /> next turn with no increase in difficulty.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can only come out of frenzy once the trigger is gone, but Berserker makes you able to enter without a trigger... So how and when does the Berserker frenzy end? Can you end it at will too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-29-2024, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T22:38:38-07:00","id":1537851,"title":"","content":"It would presumably end when whatever you wanted to go berserk for was no longer there. Even if you didn't use a Rage roll to get there, you probably still had a purpose in letting it loose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T00:22:31-07:00","id":1537852,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in the event of the Berserker merit, I would ask the player what the trigger for the Berserker rampage is when they activate it. They tell me and then we go from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T07:32:14-07:00","id":1537894,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T20:01:31-07:00","id":1538188,"title":"","content":"General question on Frenzy, how do interact the rulings that set your Frenzy successes at a specific number?<br /> <br /> For example, the <b>Mars Midsky</b> merit makes you frenzy with 2 successes, at Rank 5/6 you frenzy at 5/6+ successes,<b> Rite of the Silver Forge</b> makes you frenzy at 6 successes.<br /> <br /> I have used the ruling that Rank and Silver Forge are meant to increase the number of successes needed, not set a value (so Rite of the Silver Forge + Rank 5/6 still has a benefit) but would like to confirm.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> I would like to read your opinions, especially you Saur Ops, since I have found your comments on<b> Mars Midsky</b> on several threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-06-2024, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T22:23:37-07:00","id":1538195,"title":"","content":"Those should generally be taken as more like one more or less success to frenzy (or more), yes. Also, Mars Midsky and anything else that presently says that it frenzies on two successes should really be set to a base of three, since they were all calibrated according to W:tA 1st edition, where it only took three successes to frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}